cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Everettian Decoherence in Lean"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dalimier
    given-names: Bertrand
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    city: Nogent-sur-Marne
    country: FR
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2457-375X"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of finite quantitative projector-commutator geometry,
  including exact two-cell rigidity at cut-envelope saturation,
  cardinality- and dimension-free near-saturation stability, the finite
  coefficient-18 estimate, asymptotic coefficients 8 and 4, and a continuous
  two-parameter C3 sharpness family interpolating the coefficient
  4/max{x,1-x}. The release also contains the earlier ED1-ED4B and T1-T5
  finite formalization chain. It introduces no time dynamics or physical
  decoherence model.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - orthogonal projections
  - subspace gaps
  - operator norm
  - commutator inequalities
  - rigidity
  - stability
  - quantum foundations
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-21
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bobart0/everettian-decoherence-lean"
